        "math_academy_id": "q-49446",
        "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall  ${cos}^{2}\u2061x+{sin}^{2}\u2061x=1.$ \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x-1}=\\frac{1}{-{sin}^{2}\u2061x}=-{csc}^{2}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}{csc}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
